(2109166, 284421, 25655, '<td valign="top">What a wonderful photo!!! I am sorry I nevr got to vote.. well, you know me :-) <br/>but this is simply a gorgeous photo! I love the playful mood and the brilliant details. What a "capture the moment"!!!<br/>This one should have been placed a lot lot higher! but who asks me anyway...<br/></td>', 'What a wonderful photo!!! I am sorry I nevr got to vote.. well, you know me :-) but this is simply a gorgeous photo! I love the playful mood and the brilliant details. What a "capture the moment"!!!This one should have been placed a lot lot higher! but who asks me anyway...', '2006-02-01 07:38:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109207, 285064, 1280, '<td valign="top">Great one!  Really nice.</td>', 'Great one!  Really nice.', '2006-02-01 07:49:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109232, 285600, 10413, '<td valign="top">We were almost side by side on this one. :) Our predictions were off a little though. :)  I love the rich warm colors in this one. Nice shot!</td>', 'We were almost side by side on this one. :) Our predictions were off a little though. :)  I love the rich warm colors in this one. Nice shot!', '2006-02-01 07:56:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2109250, 285543, 48245, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the comments. I really didn''t want to post this picture as the picture I "was" trying to get was of some turkey vultures consuming a dead deer. I felt I could get a good picture of them if I could get close enough but everytime I tried they would fly away. Even parked myself near the site for over an hour trying....<br/> <br/>This deer is actually part of a large heard that roams my neighborhood. I was lucky to run into him at the time of the challenge. Actually, for the same problem as the vultures I couldn''t get close enough to get a close shot so as some of you noticed this shot looks processed because I had to really crop into it. <br/> <br/>This only argues that I really, really, really need a telephoto lens for my camera. Looking at the 70-200l lens now ;-).</td>', 'Thank you for the comments. I really didn''t want to post this picture as the picture I "was" trying to get was of some turkey vultures consuming a dead deer. I felt I could get a good picture of them if I could get close enough but everytime I tried they would fly away. Even parked myself near the site for over an hour trying.... This deer is actually part of a large heard that roams my neighborhood. I was lucky to run into him at the time of the challenge. Actually, for the same problem as the vultures I couldn''t get close enough to get a close shot so as some of you noticed this shot looks processed because I had to really crop into it.  This only argues that I really, really, really need a telephoto lens for my camera. Looking at the 70-200l lens now ;-).', '2006-02-01 08:00:24.000000', NULL, 0),
