(2110619, 284676, 42715, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by AzCKelly:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow, very nice, You can almost see him contemplating. Very nice. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you so much.  That is exactly the reason I chose this picture over the others.  I just loved the expression on his face and body.</td>', 'Originally posted by AzCKelly: Wow, very nice, You can almost see him contemplating. Very nice.   Thank you so much.  That is exactly the reason I chose this picture over the others.  I just loved the expression on his face and body.', '2006-02-01 13:04:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2110636, 284676, 42715, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by macrothing:</b></div><hr/><i> 8 - Good capture, nice colors, good composition.  Criticism; a little more detail, although I realize you may have intentionally gone for this ''softness''. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you!  The softness wasn''t intentional nor desired.  You are right in that a sharper image would be been better.  I should have done more post-editing.  Unfortunately, at 300mm focal length without a tripod, this picture is the only one with his expression and clarity that I had that wasn''t blurry!  I''ll have to remember to bring a tripod next time!  Thank you for your helpful comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by macrothing: 8 - Good capture, nice colors, good composition.  Criticism; a little more detail, although I realize you may have intentionally gone for this ''softness''.   Thank you!  The softness wasn''t intentional nor desired.  You are right in that a sharper image would be been better.  I should have done more post-editing.  Unfortunately, at 300mm focal length without a tripod, this picture is the only one with his expression and clarity that I had that wasn''t blurry!  I''ll have to remember to bring a tripod next time!  Thank you for your helpful comment.', '2006-02-01 13:08:28.000000', NULL, 0),
