(2156347, 284420, 36158, '<td valign="top">Never give up shooting...</td>', 'Never give up shooting...', '2006-02-16 10:02:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2166256, 285695, 26464, '<td valign="top">i like the texture and monotone treatment of this one</td>', 'i like the texture and monotone treatment of this one', '2006-02-20 17:25:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2173009, 285740, 39988, '<td valign="top">I lived in Colorado back in the late 80''s and miss this scenery very much.  Nice backround</td>', 'I lived in Colorado back in the late 80''s and miss this scenery very much.  Nice backround', '2006-02-22 16:56:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2179996, 285311, 49873, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! great catch.</td>', 'Congratulations! great catch.', '2006-02-24 16:21:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2181801, 284524, 7322, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by keegbow:</b></div><hr/><i> This is great image highly underated. Reminds me of the <a href="//www.nhm.ac.uk/visit-us/whats-on/temporary-exhibitions/wpy/gallery/image.jsp?image=3530" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">BBC Wildlife Photographer of the year</a>.<br/> <br/>Your in good company ! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for sharing that...After reading the photographer''s description of how he got the shot (two-fisted photography--jeesh!) I feel better about how my turned out. I wasn''t planning on taking any photos. I actually pulled over in my car to get the shot. It was really difficult because the move so bloody fast and the camera I have is practically a toy compared to what a lot of folks use on this site these days. <br/> <br/>My daughter and I had to dodge a rain of birdshit too. That was something I didn''t consider when I got out of the car. Miraculously, we were unharmed.</td>', 'Originally posted by keegbow: This is great image highly underated. Reminds me of the BBC Wildlife Photographer of the year. Your in good company !   Thanks for sharing that...After reading the photographer''s description of how he got the shot (two-fisted photography--jeesh!) I feel better about how my turned out. I wasn''t planning on taking any photos. I actually pulled over in my car to get the shot. It was really difficult because the move so bloody fast and the camera I have is practically a toy compared to what a lot of folks use on this site these days.  My daughter and I had to dodge a rain of birdshit too. That was something I didn''t consider when I got out of the car. Miraculously, we were unharmed.', '2006-02-25 10:38:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2201286, 284420, 20530, '<td valign="top">We built my parents their first computer. My dad is an outdoorsman; so I used this image for his desktop. I tried to explain how to change it if he chose, but he would have none of it. His response was "I''m NEVER going to change it!"<br/> <br/>Just wanted you to know that your patience and skill has served to make an old man in Colorado very happy.</td>', 'We built my parents their first computer. My dad is an outdoorsman; so I used this image for his desktop. I tried to explain how to change it if he chose, but he would have none of it. His response was "I''m NEVER going to change it!" Just wanted you to know that your patience and skill has served to make an old man in Colorado very happy.', '2006-03-05 10:55:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2205173, 284436, 47852, '<td valign="top">The other commenters have hit on some of the key aspects of why this shot scored so low.  The water in the background is overexposed which is distracting, and the whole shot seems to be slightly out of focus.  This comes across as a photo that you took quickly as the geese were wandering away, which you then cropped the best you could.  I know it''s hard when you''re trying to get shots of animals, but I think this would have turned out better if you had gotten at a slightly lower angle (to avoid the overexposed water) and used a shallower dof to make the geese stand out against a fuzzy background.  Hope this is helpful.</td>', 'The other commenters have hit on some of the key aspects of why this shot scored so low.  The water in the background is overexposed which is distracting, and the whole shot seems to be slightly out of focus.  This comes across as a photo that you took quickly as the geese were wandering away, which you then cropped the best you could.  I know it''s hard when you''re trying to get shots of animals, but I think this would have turned out better if you had gotten at a slightly lower angle (to avoid the overexposed water) and used a shallower dof to make the geese stand out against a fuzzy background.  Hope this is helpful.', '2006-03-06 17:50:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2213381, 284997, 54193, '<td valign="top">Great composition. I love the reflection and symetry. The water it''s standing in is a perfect frame filler... nothing distracting and nothing pulling attention away from the flamingo. It has an "art" feel to it, and would make a great print.</td>', 'Great composition. I love the reflection and symetry. The water it''s standing in is a perfect frame filler... nothing distracting and nothing pulling attention away from the flamingo. It has an "art" feel to it, and would make a great print.', '2006-03-09 01:35:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2228136, 284349, 34659, '<td valign="top">I''ve seen this shot before!  :-)  Love the composition.  The focus could be a tad sharper and I think with a little selective burning you could make it pop a bit more.  Nice capture.</td>', 'I''ve seen this shot before!  :-)  Love the composition.  The focus could be a tad sharper and I think with a little selective burning you could make it pop a bit more.  Nice capture.', '2006-03-14 21:34:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2237357, 284142, 46423, '<td valign="top">Hi Buddy!<br/>I''m thinking of getting my hands on Tamron AF 18-200mm f/3.5-6.3 XR Di II for my Canon 20D. How good this lens is?<br/>Thanks.<br/>Slav_K</td>', 'Hi Buddy!I''m thinking of getting my hands on Tamron AF 18-200mm f/3.5-6.3 XR Di II for my Canon 20D. How good this lens is?Thanks.Slav_K', '2006-03-18 10:48:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2240998, 285152, 9581, '<td valign="top">Just hanging out? Now that is not somewhere I want  to be close to...watching the history or national geo channels, I have seen enough attachs by them to make me be afraid.....<br/>Awesome picture... Love the greens and the focal points here..<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-03-20 03:54:32.</i></td>', 'Just hanging out? Now that is not somewhere I want  to be close to...watching the history or national geo channels, I have seen enough attachs by them to make me be afraid.....Awesome picture... Love the greens and the focal points here..', '2006-03-20 03:53:34.000000', '2006-03-20 03:54:32.000000', 0),
